{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION to my previous comment, so it is not read as more than it is: this ticket's signature is a SLOW failure (312-381s, requests=3), whereas the 2876 misroute fails in 0.2s at authentication. They are different failure modes and the 401s are NOT the timeouts described here.\n\nWhat survives: the misroute means an unknown share of overlap-judge calls in pre-fix runs went to a different provider than the one they were recorded against, and every judge failure — fast or slow — is swallowed as a silent abstain (`judge_one`/`judge_batch` catch Exception). So pre-fix ABSTAIN counts are contaminated and the provider attribution on them is unreliable. The 312-381s timeouts remain unexplained by 2876 and still need their own root cause."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786102353736146001,"uuid":"b270e6ad-88c7-4939-8263-ec3765623e4c"}